    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 tests pass (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `telephoneDisplay` field that renders the stored E.164 `telephone` in a human-friendly form while leaving `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`E164Telephone.java`** \u2014 Added `toDisplay(String e164)`, which splits off the country code (using the existing known-country-code table, longest prefix first) and emits `\"+<cc> <national digits grouped in threes>\"`, e.g. `\"+61412345678\"` \u2192 `\"+61 412 345 678\"`. It returns `null` for `null` and defensively returns the input unchanged if it isn't `+`-then-digits.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired a `formatTelephoneDisplay(owner)` mapping (consistent with the other derived fields like `displayName`/`initials`) that delegates to `E164Telephone.toDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` confirms `telephone` stays `+61412345678` and `telephoneDisplay` is `+61 412 345 678`.",
