    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe structure is clean and matches the codebase's existing conventions closely.\n\n- The core formatting logic (`toDisplay`) lives in `E164Telephone`, the natural home for E.164 domain knowledge. It sits right alongside `normalize`/`isValid` and reuses the existing `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` map for country-code splitting rather than duplicating that knowledge in the mapper. That's exactly where a maintainer would look for it.\n- `OwnerMapper.formatTelephoneDisplay` is a thin, consistent wrapper that delegates to `E164Telephone.toDisplay`, mirroring the existing `normalizeTelephone` delegation and the null-owner-guard pattern shared by every other `formatXxx(owner)` method. No telephone-formatting logic leaks into the mapper.\n- The `@Mapping` entry is added in the same expression style as its siblings, and the OpenAPI `telephoneDisplay` field is documented in the same shape as the neighboring derived fields (`readOnly`, title/description/example), keeping `telephone` as raw E.164 per the spec.\n\nNo duplication, no catch-all accretion, logic is in the right unit.",
